I just ascended Martha the Monk, after a ridiculous number of dumb moves on 
my part. The ability to save and think saved my ass more than once. I'd 
wanted to do this one genoless, but after at least the third time a MF/MMF 
sucked my brain and I'd already remapped the whole dungeon once *and* my 
spell of ID had expired and the spellbook was too faint to read again, all 
this before I'd even taken on Rodney, I gave up on the conduct and geno-ed 
(after blessing and reading one no-longer-identified scroll which was Remove 
Curse and another which was Confuse Monster or somesuch) h-es.

This game had nothing special early, except for altars (unattended) on DL8 
and DL17 or so, which I converted. Saw two huge leprechaun halls, which got 
my Protection to AC 1 naked and, since I had a =TC, I used to give me 
teleportitis. Early saccing on DL8 got me Mojo and Giantslayer; I stashed 
the other two and used Mojo pretty much throughout. Quest was around DL4, in 
the Rogue level. At this point I was maybe XL12, and nowhere near ready even 
to check out the first level. I continued to DL17 and found the altar, and 
set up an initial stash and polyfodder there. I +CreateMonster-ed a lot, got 
Trollsbane or somesuch when I was only hoping to see whether I could pray, 
then shortly thereafter got crowned. Ludios wasn't in this dungeon, and 
neither were any significant throne rooms (one way early [no wish], nothing 
else) or swamps or other special rooms. There was one sink before the 
castle. Medusa was the center island, easy with =Lev at around AC -10, no 
significantly great armor. Got to the castle without a /Striking on hand, so 
I did it from the back and ducked down into the VoD to find the /Striking to 
get the drawbridge open. Castle wand was at 0:3. After another few rounds of 
polypiling at the VoD altar, I wished for a scrolls, [CoMR, [HoB. I'd found 
speed boots, water walking boots, and GoP somewhere. I enchanted the CoMR, 
speed boots, and HoB up to +5 apiece, did some potion alchemy and got my 
native Int up to 18. At this point my AC was around -24 with a shield, -20 
without, for spellcasting. HP were around 120. I went back up to do the 
initial levels of the quest and stopped before Master Kaen's level.

Back down. Gehennom wasn't terrible with +Magic Mapping, even at 65% fail 
(with HoB, Int 18, no shield, leather gloves). An "AoLS saved me when a 
nymph stole my =Levitation on Juiblex's level, though IMO since I could 
teleport at will (leprechaun) and had intrinsic TC, it shouldn't have 
counted as a death-- even without the amulet the character would have 
survived.

Found the VS easily, took Vlad out, came back up to do the quest. Before the 
quest, I wished for another magic marker, alchemized so more to around 240 
HP and AC -37 and thought about wishing for a /Death, since (a) Juiblex's 
had exploded and (b) I still had them identified after the first big MF 
thing. I decided to go with +Sleep and +Magic Missle instead, and that 
turned out so well that I suspect that I'd overprepared. 

After the Quest I was ready to get Rodney and head out. And this is where 
all hell, NPI, broke loose. 

Something in the second level of Rodney's castle summoned and summoned, and 
something else had a /Create Monster. I got sucked and sucked and ended up 
backed into a corner with a =Conflict, hoping that I'd heal faster than 
damage was being handed out. While the horde was =Conflicting, I blessed and 
read the three un-IDed scrolls mentioned above and genocided hs. Without the 
MF risk, the rest of the horde was easy. With almost nothing identified any 
more, I recharged my /Wishing and wished for a /Death. Also wished for a 
+Magic Mapping, since mine was too faded to read and I accidentally thought 
that the spell was timed out. After using the wish I learned that I'd 
misread the list of spells the last time I'd gone to cast Mapping, and I'd 
still had it in memory. 

Rodney went down to the /Death.

More trouble from Rodney on the way down to Moloch's-- once? twice? he came 
back. Since I wasn't sure how many charges the wand had, I wanted to 
conserve it and fought Rodney at least once. As long as I had the Remove 
Curse spell, I figured that there was nothing too terrible he could do to 
me.

Moloch's was easy, and the cursed !GL got me out.

Heading back up, all was fine until in Orcus's town a Titan or something 
summoned, at around the same time a random curse hit, and suddenly my Bag of 
Holding was cursed and I couldn't cast Remove Curse because Mojo or my 
gloves were cursed as well and I couldn't dip the Bag because I was too 
overloaded. I panicked and saved and considered abandoning the game since it 
seemed clear that I was being outfought consistently. Came back, dropped the 
Bag and the Amulet, and trekked back to the VoD at DL26 for a /Cancellation 
and some food, since all my food was in the Bag. (All I had in my Oilskin 
bag outside the BoH was a few holy waters, a few full healing, and two 
?Remove Curse which I don't know why I didn't think of.) Came back, 
cancelled the BoH, dipped it, all was fine, and I was able to fight the 
horde without a real problem. Everything seemed to get easier from this 
point out.

Got pulled back a lot after this little bit-- 30-31(Orcus), 31-32 ,32 ,30-
31, 30-31 ,30-31, 31-32.

Heading up, I used the Eyes of the Underworld as a substitute for Magic 
Mapping as much as possible. Used a randomly-found cockatrice corpse (well, 
a corpse from a randomly-generated cockatrice) to take out Rodney on Earth. 
Used confused ?Gold Detection on the first three planes, got my unihorn 
randomly cursed, discovered that my Remove Curse spell had timed out (used 
holy water instead on the unihorn), so I reread the spellbook in a vortex or 
somesuch on Air, and wrote a last ?Gold Detection there as well. The Plane 
of Water went faster than usual, and even without ; genocided they didn't 
seem to be much of a problem.

Arrived on Astral not wearing the =Conflict, got an Angel. Headed right, 
toward Death, and was being hit hard, so I put the =Conflict on. Right altar 
was lawful, IIRC. Next tried the middle, with Famine. Middle was chaotic. 
Finally dealt with Pestilence, which made me sick once, and headed left to 
offer the Amulet to Chih Sung-tzu. 

A choir sang, I was bathed in radiance, and all that. 


